+# Issue #43 — patch for the uploaded complete project
+
+This patch targets the exact `lut.cn.c2cplatform` source in `c2csectrade(1).zip`.
+It does not apply to the different `sg.edu.nus.iss.c2csectrade` GitHub implementation.
+Only order/expiry code, transaction acceptance tests and their Maven configuration
+are included. Existing recommendation, credit, chat, media and frontend features
+are not copied or replaced.
+
+## Apply and validate
+
+From the root containing the uploaded project's `pom.xml`:
+
+```sh
+git apply --check /path/to/issue43-uploaded-project.patch
+git apply /path/to/issue43-uploaded-project.patch
+mvn verify
+```
+
+Use JDK 17, Maven and a running Docker daemon. `mvn verify` runs unit tests,
+MySQL Testcontainers integration tests, then JaCoCo report and coverage check.
+For a unit-only check without Docker, use `mvn verify -DskipITs`. That command
+is **not** proof that real database tests passed.
+
+## Acceptance mapping
+
+| Requirement | Checks |
+|---|---|
+| Success for four payment methods; correct recorded method | `OrderAcceptanceTest`, `TransactionAcceptanceIT` |
+| Wrong PIN and insufficient balance refused | Both suites; MySQL assertions verify rollback of prior stock updates |
+| Invalid confirm/cancel/payment transitions refused | `OrderAcceptanceTest.invalidTransitionsAreRefused`; repeated payment/completion checks |
+| Paid order never expired, including stale scan results | `OrderExpiryAcceptanceTest.rechecksCandidatesAfterPaymentWinsAndSkipsNonExpiredRows`; `TransactionAcceptanceIT.successfulPaymentDeductsStockOnceAndCannotBeExpired` |
+| Repeated expiry is safe | `OrderExpiryAcceptanceTest`, `TransactionAcceptanceIT.repeatedExpiryNeverInflatesStock` |
+| Non-completed and duplicate review refused | `ReviewAcceptanceTest`; DELIVERED and COMPLETED remain accepted as in uploaded code |
+| Concurrent payment cannot deduct twice | `TransactionAcceptanceIT.concurrentPaymentsHaveOneWinnerAndOneLedgerRow` |
+
+The uploaded checkout does not reserve/deduct stock or remove cart items until
+payment. Therefore expiry cannot release a separate reservation: none exists in
+this model. The fix leaves stock and cart untouched instead of inventing inventory
+or increasing existing cart quantities. It locks and rechecks each candidate row.
+Payment, completion and cancellation take the same order row lock; read-only order
+lookup keeps its existing interface. The expiry transaction no longer swallows
+write failures, allowing Spring to roll it back.
+
+The transaction integration context uses the uploaded `init.sql`, real mapper XML
+and real Spring transaction proxies. It stubs only credit scoring (outside this
+issue); it does not mock order, stock, wallet persistence or the transaction manager.
+External Redis/MinIO/RabbitMQ servers are unnecessary for this focused context.
+
+## Coverage and scope limits
+
+The per-class JaCoCo gate requires 81% line coverage on the three implementations
+actually exercised here: `OrderServiceImpl`, `ReviewServiceImpl`, `OrderExpireTask`.
+It is not an application-wide coverage figure or branch-coverage claim.
+
+Neither the uploaded source nor its documentation identifies the five design
+problems/classes referenced by #43. This patch does not invent that list or replace
+the uploaded architecture to manufacture five patterns. That acceptance criterion
+must be mapped to the team's actual design list before #43 can be marked fully done.
+
+Existing behavior outside this issue remains: sellers are credited at confirmation,
+reviews permit both DELIVERED and COMPLETED, and cancellation has its own existing
+cart-handling behavior. The patch does not introduce a new payment/state architecture.
